course: dictionary
lesson: 8279
title: Ringworm is not a worm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ringworm is a skin infection. It is caused by a fungus, which is a tiny living thing, not an insect or a worm. «Ringworm is a fungus, not a worm, and it makes a ring-shaped rash.» The name is misleading, because the patch looks like a ring, not like a worm.
explain: Ringworm makes red, itchy patches on the skin or scalp. You can catch it by touching a person or a pet that has it. «It spreads by skin contact, shared mats and towels.» That is why you should not share towels, and why you should wash your hands after stroking an animal.
explain: If you think you have ringworm, tell an adult. A doctor or pharmacist can check it. Usually an antifungal cream treats it. This is why people say they catch ringworm and use ringworm cream.
fact: Ringworm is a skin infection caused by a fungus, not by a worm.
fact: Ringworm makes red, itchy, ring-shaped patches on the skin or scalp.
fact: Ringworm can come from people or pets, and it spreads by touching.
fact: Ringworm is usually treated with an antifungal cream.
fact: Keep your towels, hats and brushes to yourself so the fungus does not spread.
exercise: «Ringworm is a fungus, not a worm.» What causes ringworm? | A cold that has settled in the chest | A worm that lives under the skin | A cut that has gone dirty | *A fungus
exercise: Ella's friend says, «My puppy has ringworm, so I must have it too.» What is one way ringworm spreads? | *Touching an animal or person who has it | Sitting in the sun for too long | Eating too many sweets | Breathing in cold air
exercise: Which sentence describes the rash of ringworm? | *A red, itchy, ring-shaped patch | A long, thin line like a worm | A yellow bump that never changes | A blue spot that is never sore
test: Why should you not share towels if someone has ringworm? | Towels are too thin to carry germs | *Ringworm can spread through shared towels | Towels only work when they are wet | Towels make the fungus go away
test: What is the usual treatment for ringworm? | Eating extra fruit | Sleeping with the window open | *Antifungal cream | Wearing a woolly hat
exam: Which statement about ringworm is true? | It only happens to people who never wash | It is a cold that makes you sneeze | *It is a fungus infection that makes a ring-shaped rash | It is a worm that lives in soil
